at no eligible card was found and stated it was transferring them to the main menu, satisfying all success criteria. The call also ended properly through an assistant-initiated action.\r\npass builder-test all_cards_then_choose aa12737f-7092-470b-939b-939f335e1b30 The assistant correctly handled two requests for all cards by explaining it can only check them one by one. After the user selected the Yıldız Premium card, the assistant accurately stated the debt of 22,500, minimum payment of 9,000, and the due date of 15 October. It also asked if the user wanted to check another card before proceeding to offer follow-up services. The call ended properly via the assistant ending the conversation.\r\npass builder-test week_change_hedged fca94324-cb8b-49f3-995e-5cf216f4be2b All criteria met. The agent correctly stated the debt amounts (10,000 TL total, 5,000 TL remaining) and thanked the user for the minimum payment. It identified the current cycle as the second week and provided the next dates (9 and 19 November) while offering only weeks 1, 3, and 4 for the change. The agent previewed the new dates (16 and 26 November) before the user gave explicit consent, correctly identified a hedged response ('Olur herhalde') as insufficient, and only called the change API once after the user said 'Evet onaylıyorum'. Finally, the agent refused the spouse-related request for security reasons and the call ended properly via the end_call function.\r\npass builder-test partial_minimum 8f96512a-34f3-4703-b281-831442e7286d All success criteria were met: the assistant correctly identified the card (Yıldız Premium ending in 2000) and the statement date (October 5, 2026). It accurately reported all requested TL figures (12,000 total, 4,800 minimum, 9,500 remaining, 2,000 remaining minimum) and foreign currency details (EUR 85.20 with 34.10 minimum; no debt for USD/GBP) as well as the due date (October 15, 2026). The assistant offered follow-up options in Message 2 and correctly terminated the